Z||000001||Fformula88||11-26-2000||12:03 AM||||What is the attraction?<P>The Fiero is quick, fun to drive, handles GREAT, gets tone of LOOKS, is still stylish 12 years after it was produce... need I go on???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I do as much work as I can on my Fiero.  I had a DEALER service department sabatoge it to try to get extra money out of e for service  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  I do not trust many mechanics, and besides... I love that great feeling when I can figure out the problem and fix it myself!<P>Congrats on ressurecting your Fiero!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||11-26-2000||12:39 AM||||I just like the car. Bought one new in 1986, got rid of it in 1991, Friend bought one in 1994, By 1995 I had another 1986 Fiero!<BR>I do all the work myself. With all the time and money invested I wouldn't trust the car to anyone else. I've even spent over 20 minutes arguing with the EPA testing people when they wanted to test it with one if their people driving it on the rollers. (looks like a dyno machine) I ended up driving it. Now I don't have to worry. (It's exempt from future testing since it's insured as a collectable).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-26-2000||08:37 AM||||Hormones.  It's lust, pure and simple.  There are alot of good looking cars out there, but none of them are a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||11-26-2000||07:20 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/red84.jpg"> <P>I got this as my first car. It was very gutless (probably due to a plugged cat) but I liked it anyway. I have an 86 GT now, but I liked my 84 better. I don't pay other people to fix what I can fix myself. Most of my problems are from lack of tools. I also need to get my car aligned so that's another thing that I need to have someone else do.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Patrick's Dad||11-26-2000||10:04 PM||||Bob, in everyone's life, they have something that they fancy. It might be beer, coffee, Barbie dolls, or gullwing Jaguars. We have Fieros, and so do you. They are unique, attainable, repairable, and customizable.<P>Cars in general are a guy thing, I think mostly because when they break, you can figure them out and fix them. Not so with women, Mary in particular.<P>Just live with it, and enjoy. And bring the d**n jack over so I can drain my car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000006||2xsess||11-27-2000||07:54 PM||||I don't know why I love the Fiero, I just do. Maybe it's the styling or the handling or the torque. Well...take your pick. lol<P><BR>I do as much of the work as I can myself. Of course there are certain things I can't do either due to lack of experience tools or space. <P>Congrats on the resurection of you Fiero.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
