Z||000010||PearlBlueSoul||11-29-2000||05:04 PM||||Heheh, we just finished having this discussion some time ago....hehe.<BR>Why do I like my car so much?  lemme find my reply to that thread and it'll explain everything.&gt;&gt;<P><B>First reply:</B><BR>Gotta admit, even though I'm not driving my car, I just go down to it and look it over for a few minutes. even just one minute. I get the biggest stupid grin on my face from seeing that car, or other MR2s. Even beat-to-****  ones. It's like, a lineage of sorts. It's strange how attached I've gotten to this car, I mean, when my parents ask me what I'd get to replace it I can't think of a single car that could match it in ANYTHING. It's, just something you can't describe. I guess it's love, because you can't define that either. <P><B>second reply to the same thread:::</B><P>heheh...I know I got pulled over running a red light while trying to catch up with a white MKII that was gonig the other way. hehe. There was a light a good 1/8th mile away that had just turned yellow, and the MR2 had just passed under it. I said, "I can do this." I got half way there, and the light went red, I was like, "Well, maybe not." I tried slamming on the brakes, and they started to squeal. As I did this, I looked up and through the cross street I saw a cop sitting at the light. I froze. Somehow, my brake foot came off the pedal and I glided right on through.  She let me off tho, as I had no prior history, and obviously was a nervous wreck. This, about 3 weeks away from the court date that would take my license.  <P>it's wierd, every time I see one I call it out, "MR2!" and everyone's like, "What??" "A MR2 went that way :: points ::." "Oh." I swear, every time one passes me, I always look up just in time to see it go by. I bout lost it when I saw one that had the 94-95 taillight conversion. When GT came out I saw the revised rear fascia, and didn't know that was what they looked like; I thought they had gotten it wrong. Then I saw one on the road and went nuts, drooling inside the car as I watched it motor down the road. no one else seemed to care. hehe. <P>Like I said, I think these cars become family after a while somehow. It's love for sure.<BR> <BR><B>Amother member posted this...</B><BR>Happiness is knowing that your 2 will be there, no matter what, girlfriends change, friends change, but the MR2 will always be there to put a smile on your face.<P><B> ...to which i replied:</B><BR>you've no idea how many times i've thought the same thing. At times when I was most down and out, I thought about that alot. I'd walk out to my car, get in, and just drive. not knowing where, no where in particular...just driving. it's a very nice thing to just get into something you like so much and staying in it for a long time. <P>Like taking a hot bath, so is driving my 2. I get in and just sit there for a long, long time.<P><P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Joe4x4||11-29-2000||05:44 PM||||I bought my first Fiero last year after my Camero died on me . I needed a another car to get to work and back.<BR>There was this Fiero in a used car lot <BR>(86 se)..I bought it for $ 500 .<BR>computer went on me  6 month`s later ...so I bought a 2 nd one for part (84 se).<BR>As I was bring that one home ..there was a message on my anawesring machine , this black 86 se with V-6 and viper alarm on it <BR>which I loohed at a week before.( he said I`ll sell it to you for $ 600 .<BR>he wanted $1,200 for it )<BR>So need I say more I bought it ..hehehe<P>Now I have 3 ...<BR>Boy I like these little cars.<BR>looking at putting a V-8 in one of them <BR>and running it down Atco raceway N.J.<BR>||||reg||6
